.TH setboot 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
setboot \- show or set the boot command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setboot
.I device
.br
.B setboot
.I device
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
The first sector of a FUZIX filesystem has room for a short command
line, which the kernel reads at boot and passes to
.BR init .
.B setboot
prints what is there, or writes a new one.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I device
The block device holding the filesystem, not the mount point.
.TP
.I command
Up to 63 characters.  Longer is refused.
.SH NOTES
With no command set,
.B setboot
says
.BR "No command set." .
.PP
This writes to block 0 of the device.  Getting the device wrong writes
over the start of the wrong filesystem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR telinit (1),
.BR reboot (1),
.BR prtroot (1)
